{
  "name": "Clip new YouTube uploads into viral shorts with open-source OpenShorts and publish after Telegram approval",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note-overview",
      "name": "Read me first",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1060,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## Clip your YouTube channel and publish after approval\n\n**Who's it for**\nCreators and small teams who publish long videos and want shorts from them without\nhanding the publish button to a machine. It suits anyone who already runs n8n and\ndoes not want to build the clipping and the multi-platform posting themselves.\n\n**What it does**\nOnce a day it reads your channel RSS feed and picks one video: your newest upload,\nor the next unprocessed one from the back catalogue. It sends that video to\nOpenShorts, which returns finished 9:16 clips with subtitles through a webhook, so\nthere is no polling loop. Each clip arrives in Telegram with Publish and Skip\nbuttons. Approved clips are scheduled one per day to the social accounts connected\nin your OpenShorts account, and every Sunday the workflow reports the impressions\nand best post of what it published.\n\n**How to set up**\n1. Create an API key at openshorts.app and add it as a Header Auth credential\n   (Name: Authorization, Value: Bearer osk_...).\n2. Create a Telegram bot with @BotFather and add the Telegram credential.\n3. Fill the three **Settings** nodes with your YouTube channel id and Telegram chat id.\n4. Copy the production URL of the *Clips ready* webhook node into the\n   `webhook_url` field of *Start OpenShorts job*.\n\n**Requirements**\nAn OpenShorts account (free tier covers 20 minutes of video a month, paid plans\nfrom $12/month) or a self-hosted instance, a Telegram bot, and an n8n reachable\nover https so Telegram can register the approval buttons.\n\n**How to customize**\nChange the schedule to clip more or less often, edit the platforms list in\n*Schedule social post*, widen the posting rhythm in *Pick next free slot*, or\nreplace the Telegram approval with your own review step."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "note-act1",
      "name": "Act 1 note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -560,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## ACT 1 — Watch the channel (daily)\n\nOnce a day this branch reads your channel's RSS feed and picks **one** video to clip: a new upload if there is one, otherwise the next unprocessed video from your back catalog (newest first). One video per day keeps your quota burn predictable.\n\n**Setup**: put your channel id in the *Channel RSS feed* node (`https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=UC...`). Find it at youtube.com → your channel → About → Share → Copy channel ID.\n\nIf OpenShorts answers 402 (out of minutes) the machine pauses and tells you on Telegram instead of failing silently."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "daily-schedule",
      "name": "Every day 09:00",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        -80,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "days",
              "triggerAtHour": 9
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "channel-rss",
      "name": "Channel RSS feed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.rssFeedRead",
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "=https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id={{ $json.youtube_channel_id }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.1
    },
    {
      "id": "pick-video",
      "name": "Pick next video",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One video per run: the newest video we have not processed yet.\n// A fresh upload is by definition the newest unprocessed one, so new\n// uploads win automatically; with nothing new, the back catalog drains\n// newest-first. Processed links persist in workflow static data\n// (production executions only — manual test runs do not save it).\nconst staticData = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');\nconst done = staticData.processedVideos || [];\nconst videos = $input.all().map((i) => i.json);\nconst fresh = videos.filter((v) => v.link && !done.includes(v.link));\nif (fresh.length === 0) {\n  return [];\n}\nconst pick = fresh[0];\nreturn [{ json: { url: pick.link, title: pick.title, published: pick.isoDate } }];"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "start-job",
      "name": "Start OpenShorts job",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput",
      "position": [
        660,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.openshorts.app/api/process",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {},
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"url\": \"{{ $json.url }}\",\n  \"acknowledged\": true,\n  \"webhook_url\": \"PASTE_THE_PRODUCTION_URL_OF_THE_CLIPS-READY_WEBHOOK_NODE_HERE\",\n  \"webhook_secret\": \"change-me\"\n}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "name": "OpenShorts API key"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "mark-processed",
      "name": "Mark video as processed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        800,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Only mark the video done once OpenShorts accepted the job — a failed\n// submit (quota, downtime) leaves it unmarked so tomorrow retries it.\nconst staticData = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');\nconst done = staticData.processedVideos || [];\nconst url = $('Pick next video').first().json.url;\nif (!done.includes(url)) {\n  done.push(url);\n}\nstaticData.processedVideos = done;\nreturn $input.all();"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
